  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "The current best (config_048, acc=0.520) uses scgpt as the RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The image-only baseline (0.260) confirms multimodal fusion is critical, and weighted fusion slightly edges out concat (0.520 vs 0.507). However, we have no evidence on whether scgpt is the optimal RNA encoder. config_003 is a clean single-variable swap: it replaces scgpt with scvi_n200 while keeping all other settings identical to the current best (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal). This directly tests whether the learned generative RNA representation (scgpt) is meaningfully superior to the variational autoencoder (scvi_n200), reducing uncertainty on a fundamental architectural choice before committing remaining budget to fine-tuning aggregation or image encoder variants."
}

